{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping you today. You're here to have a peritoneal dialysis catheter placed, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been on hemodialysis for a while now, but I’d like to switch to peritoneal dialysis if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve been doing well with your AV fistula, but you want more independence with your dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. I’ve been managing okay, but the clinic visits are hard on my schedule. I’d like to try doing it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your nephrologist and gastroenterologist have both approved this, and your stomach symptoms are under control?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my gastroparesis has been better lately. I haven’t had much nausea or bloating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll be doing a laparoscopic procedure tomorrow morning to place the catheter in your abdomen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt? I’m a bit nervous about the surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a minimally invasive surgery, so recovery is usually quicker. You’ll be under general anesthesia, so you won’t feel anything during the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And afterward? How bad will the pain be?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most patients have mild to moderate discomfort. We’ll give you hydrocodone for pain as needed, and you’ll use an incentive spirometer to help with breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds manageable. What about my other medications? Should I keep taking them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve restarted all your home medications. Fluoxetine, gabapentin, insulin — everything stays the same unless we adjust it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been on insulin for years, so I’m used to it. But I do get anxious sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you’re on clonazepam for anxiety. You can take it as needed, and we’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I also have some fatigue and numbness from diabetes, but it’s been stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your neuropathy and fatigue are noted. We’ll make sure you’re not overexerting yourself post-op."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my eyes — I have some diabetic retinopathy. Should I be worried about that affecting recovery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s managed by your eye doctor. It doesn’t affect the surgery, but it’s important to keep up with those checkups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2180-03-06 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I just want to make sure everything’s covered."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2180-03-06 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set for surgery tomorrow morning. We’ll see you in the OR around 8 AM."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2180-03-06 18:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I’ll rest up tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You came through the surgery well. You now have a Tenckhoff catheter placed in your abdomen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, it’s already done? I didn’t feel a thing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it went smoothly. In the recovery room, we noticed a little bleeding from the exit site, but we held pressure and it stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bleeding? Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A small amount of oozing can happen. We’ve replaced the dressing, and it’s not active now. We’ll watch it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s reassuring. I also remember someone telling me to take deep breaths."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your oxygen levels dipped a bit, but they came back up when you breathed deeply. We gave you a little oxygen for a few hours, but you’re off it now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had sleep apnea for years. Could that be why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2180-03-07 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. That’s why we encourage deep breathing and using the incentive spirometer — to keep your lungs clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2180-03-07 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just finished your hemodialysis session. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2180-03-07 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pretty good. No cramps or dizziness. My fistula did fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2180-03-07 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your blood pressure is a bit lower than yesterday — 102 over 56 — but you’re not symptomatic, so that’s okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2180-03-07 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve always had low blood pressure. As long as I’m not fainting, I’m used to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you today. You’re doing well — pain is controlled, you’re eating, and your oxygen levels are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us if you develop fevers over 101, chills, or increasing abdominal pain. Also, don’t remove the dressing — the PD nurse will check it in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I keep taking my regular meds, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. All your medications continue, including insulin, gabapentin, and pantoprazole. The hydrocodone is only for pain as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your nephrologist in two weeks, and the PD nurse will help you start training on using the catheter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’m ready to get started with this new phase."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2180-03-07 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. We’ll get your discharge papers ready, and you can go home soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2180-03-07 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave — your abdomen is soft, no redness at the site, and you’re walking fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2180-03-07 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2180-03-07 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy for the next few days, and don’t hesitate to call if anything seems off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2180-03-07 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m looking forward to starting peritoneal dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2180-03-07 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll support you every step of the way. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2180-03-07 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2180-03-06 16:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2180-03-07 20:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted electively to transition from hemodialysis to peritoneal dialysis. She underwent an uncomplicated laparoscopic placement of a Tenckhoff peritoneal dialysis catheter. Postoperatively, she experienced minor oozing from the catheter site that resolved with pressure, and transient oxygen desaturation that improved with encouragement to deep breathe and supplemental oxygen, which was weaned off by the next day. She tolerated her scheduled hemodialysis session well and remained stable throughout her stay. She was discharged home with instructions to follow up with her nephrologist and PD nurse, continue all home medications, and monitor for signs of infection or complications at the catheter site.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Atrophic gastritis, without mention of hemorrhage",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
